.cm
.cs 1 on
WHICH EXEC

The 'which' command mimics the 'which' command found on most POSIX systems
such as Unix and Linux reporting the file behind the command. The output is
normally a single line, similar to the behavoir of traditional Unix 'which'.
But z/VM, and especially CMS, is a multi-token environment, so the output
is of the form filename <blank> filetype <blank> filemode.

'which' works by locating the indicated command as an EXEC or MODULE
or Pipelines gem or CP command.
.cs 1 off

.cs 2 on
'which' takes one argument, the command verb for which you are searching.
'which' allows an optional second argument indicating a specific command type.
+-----------+----------------------------------------------------------+
|   which   |   verb  [type]                                           |
+-----------+----------------------------------------------------------+
.cs 2 off

.cs 3 on
¢|Example¢%

        Ready;
        which which
        WHICH EXEC P MNT319
        Ready;

.cs 3 off

.cs 4 on
¢|Note¢%

'which' honors the settings of IMPEX and IMPCP.
It's behavior changes depending on these settings.
.cs 4 off
